        "hotel": {
            "name": "3HB Hotel Faro",
            "strapline": "Urban glamour in the Algarve’s capital",
            "description": "<p>Algarve hotels don&rsquo;t come much trendier than this gem in the heart of Faro, pairing elements of both classic and contemporary Portuguese style to achieve a sleek, urban aesthetic. It&rsquo;s far from a case of style over substance though, as it's got a top notch location, five-star facilities, and first class hospitality to boot. </p>\n<p>Head up to the rooftop terrace and you&rsquo;ll find an infinity pool, a firepit and a swanky terrace bar with gorgeous views looking out across the city&rsquo;s terracotta-tiled skyline and towards the Ria Formosa lagoon in the distance. As if that&rsquo;s not enticing enough, there&rsquo;s also a spa with a heated indoor pool, a Turkish bath and a sauna &ndash; perfect for unwinding after a day of strolling the cobblestone streets.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You&rsquo;ve also got a couple of restaurants on-site to choose from; Forno Nero, which deals in Portuguese and Italian fusion cuisine down at street level, and H&aacute;bito, up on the rooftop, where you can experience the innovative Algarve cuisine which celebrates the freshest ingredients from the region.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>As for the rooms, they&rsquo;re just as luxurious as you&rsquo;d expect. Think soft, cream-coloured tones, quality wooden furnishings, Marshall Bluetooth speakers, spacious bathrooms with walk-in showers, and super comfortable beds.&nbsp;</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>",
            "starRating": "5",
